[break] a-request-past-the-budget-is-run
rule: A request past the connection's budget is refused `overloaded` and not run, so what a client may hold is bounded.
file: crates/cortex-rpc/src/connection.rs
in: request
find: let fits = budget.requests < self.shared.options.max_requests
replace: let fits = budget.requests < usize::MAX
caught-by:
    cortex-rpc::it wire::a_client_that_floods_and_reads_nothing_is_closed

[break] refusals-are-held-without-end
rule: A client with more refusals unread than requests may run is closed: it sends and does not read.
file: crates/cortex-rpc/src/connection.rs
in: refuse
find: if budget.refusals >= self.options.max_requests.max(1) {
replace: if budget.refusals >= usize::MAX {
caught-by:
    cortex-rpc::it wire::a_client_that_floods_and_reads_nothing_is_closed

[break] a-client-that-takes-nothing-is-never-closed
rule: A client that takes no line while whole events wait past its queue's capacity is closed after `stalled_client`.
file: crates/cortex-rpc/src/connection.rs
in: send
find: || (past && waited >= options.stalled_client)
replace: || (past && waited >= Duration::MAX)
caught-by:
    cortex-rpc::it wire::a_client_that_takes_nothing_is_closed_and_the_session_goes_on

[break] the-lane-is-waited-for-before-the-client-is-disconnected
rule: A connection's end disconnects its client first, which withdraws what it was asked, and only then waits for the lane: an open waiting on a question it never answered does not hold the end.
file: crates/cortex-rpc/src/connection.rs
in: run
find:
        if let Some(client) = self.client() {
            self.shared.core.disconnect(client.id).await;
        }
        if let Some(lane) = self.dispatcher.as_mut().and_then(Dispatcher::close)
            && within(&self.shared.options.timer, self.shared.options.lane_end, lane)
                .await
                .is_none()
        {
            tracing::warn!("the connection's last operation did not end in time");
        }
replace:
        if let Some(lane) = self.dispatcher.as_mut().and_then(Dispatcher::close)
            && within(&self.shared.options.timer, self.shared.options.lane_end, lane)
                .await
                .is_none()
        {
            tracing::warn!("the connection's last operation did not end in time");
        }
        if let Some(client) = self.client() {
            self.shared.core.disconnect(client.id).await;
        }
caught-by:
    cortex-rpc::it wire::a_client_that_leaves_while_its_open_waits_on_a_question_ends_at_once

[break] shutdown-answers-before-the-requests-under-way
rule: `shutdown` is answered once the requests under way have ended, so an open being put together ends itself before the server does.
file: crates/cortex-rpc/src/connection.rs
in: finish
find:
        if within(&shared.options.timer, shared.options.requests_end, running)
            .await
            .is_none()
        {
            tracing::warn!("requests were still running at the server's end");
        }
        if let Some(id) = self.shutdown.take() {
            // Its place was taken when it was read.
            shared.answered(id, Ok(OpResult::Shutdown(Empty {})), Frees::Refusal);
        }
replace:
        if let Some(id) = self.shutdown.take() {
            // Its place was taken when it was read.
            shared.answered(id, Ok(OpResult::Shutdown(Empty {})), Frees::Refusal);
        }
        if within(&shared.options.timer, shared.options.requests_end, running)
            .await
            .is_none()
        {
            tracing::warn!("requests were still running at the server's end");
        }
caught-by:
    cortex-rpc::it wire::a_shutdown_waits_for_the_requests_under_way_before_it_answers

